WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:17.530
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:17.800 --> 00:20.520
They say there are no secrets in this world.

3
00:22.080 --> 00:24.880
Is it true that the people in Creative are having an affair?

4
00:25.080 --> 00:26.880
Keep your voice down.

5
00:26.880 --> 00:30.480
Walls have ears.

6
00:30.720 --> 00:34.200
Someone’s chat screenshots just got leaked yesterday.

7
00:34.520 --> 00:37.240
Come on! You can hide nothing here.

8
00:38.040 --> 00:40.240
You can, if you’re good enough.

9
00:42.440 --> 00:44.960
Do you think Dan can close the deal this time?

10
00:46.680 --> 00:47.800
I feel bad for him.

11
00:48.200 --> 00:50.920
With a budget this big, the pressure must be insane.

12
00:51.560 --> 00:54.880
But as a top-selling AE,

13
00:54.880 --> 00:56.840
I think he’ll pull it off.

14
00:57.480 --> 00:59.560
That’s true.

15
00:59.560 --> 01:01.240
Not even two years here,

16
01:01.240 --> 01:02.680
and he’s a top performer every month.

17
01:02.680 --> 01:03.360
Right.

18
01:04.959 --> 01:06.760
But my secret…

19
01:07.320 --> 01:09.640
-doesn’t even need to be dug up. -Let’s gossip after some snacks.

20
01:09.640 --> 01:11.320
It just spills out on its own

21
01:14.680 --> 01:16.039
like a nosebleed

22
01:17.280 --> 01:20.760
that strikes whenever I’m under pressure.

23
01:21.320 --> 01:24.160
And it always happens on important days.

24
01:25.320 --> 01:26.320
But whatever.

25
01:26.840 --> 01:28.800
I can handle it.

26
01:29.280 --> 01:31.240
Just wipe it away quickly,

27
01:31.600 --> 01:33.039
and no one will ever know.

28
01:33.560 --> 01:36.280
Congratulations to our scholarship student,

29
01:36.280 --> 01:38.840
Mr. Danusorn Promsri.

30
01:49.560 --> 01:51.360
I kept my secret hidden…

31
01:51.560 --> 01:53.560
to make my life look as perfect as possible.

32
01:56.479 --> 01:57.560
Stand a little closer.

33
01:57.560 --> 02:00.160
I graduated with first-class honors

34
02:00.400 --> 02:02.200
from a top university.

35
02:02.560 --> 02:04.080
Many juniors looked up to me.

36
02:04.080 --> 02:05.240
Thank you.

37
02:05.880 --> 02:07.000
P’Dan!

38
02:07.800 --> 02:09.639
Wow, is this for me?

39
02:09.880 --> 02:12.320
-Isn’t it cute? -It’s so cute and huge.

40
02:12.560 --> 02:14.760
-Thank you. -Let’s take a picture.

41
02:19.240 --> 02:20.160
P’Dan.

42
02:20.400 --> 02:22.600
Could you give us a CEO pose?

43
02:22.600 --> 02:23.960
Act cool.

44
02:24.079 --> 02:24.760
Sure.

45
02:31.280 --> 02:34.160
What kind of CEO can’t afford a cup of coffee?

46
02:36.560 --> 02:38.880
How about this pose? It’s cuter.

47
02:38.880 --> 02:40.480
It really is cute.

48
02:40.480 --> 02:42.079
Three, two, one!

49
02:42.079 --> 02:46.760
P’Dan, P’Dan, P’Dan!

50
02:58.440 --> 03:00.640
Why should we hire you?

51
03:01.120 --> 03:02.160
Honestly,

52
03:02.760 --> 03:04.040
I’d love to say…

53
03:04.520 --> 03:05.720
because I’m amazing.

54
03:06.520 --> 03:09.240
But I don’t want to get kicked out just yet, so I’ll say…

55
03:09.240 --> 03:11.480
If someone gives me an opportunity,

56
03:12.080 --> 03:13.480
I’ll make it so worthwhile

57
03:13.480 --> 03:15.400
that they’ll never regret it.

58
03:21.960 --> 03:24.320
Congratulations!

59
03:29.120 --> 03:29.840
Congrats!

60
03:29.840 --> 03:30.920
Thank you.

61
03:31.160 --> 03:32.360
Great job.

62
03:32.880 --> 03:33.800
You deserve it.

63
03:33.800 --> 03:35.000
Thank you, everyone,

64
03:35.680 --> 03:36.760
for coming to surprise me.

65
03:41.920 --> 03:43.000
These days,

66
03:43.160 --> 03:45.760
whenever people look at me, this is all they see.

67
03:47.520 --> 03:50.400
The perfect image I created.

68
04:19.519 --> 04:21.519
Nong Dan!

69
04:21.519 --> 04:22.280
Oh!

70
04:22.840 --> 04:23.720
Your shirt…

71
04:29.480 --> 04:30.680
It’s gorgeous.

72
04:30.680 --> 04:33.760
Don’t tell me it’s from the new collection.

73
04:35.720 --> 04:36.320
Yes.

74
04:36.680 --> 04:37.840
It’s the latest collection.

75
04:38.120 --> 04:39.040
Oh gosh!

76
04:39.400 --> 04:40.520
It’s fabulous.

77
04:41.560 --> 04:43.120
I’ll see you later then.

78
04:43.120 --> 04:43.880
Sure.

79
04:45.600 --> 04:47.200
How is everyone doing?

80
04:54.000 --> 04:54.800
Hello.

81
04:55.080 --> 04:56.880
I’m Dan, Danusorn Promsri,

82
04:56.880 --> 04:58.840
the Account Executive for this project.

83
04:59.840 --> 05:00.960
So, let’s get started.

84
05:01.560 --> 05:04.600
The concept for this project is ‘Driving Beyond Luxury’.

85
05:04.600 --> 05:07.720
We want to make driving more than just luxury.

86
05:08.080 --> 05:09.760
We’re keeping the luxury aspect,

87
05:09.760 --> 05:11.960
but we’ll push more driving experience.

88
05:12.280 --> 05:14.240
Our target group is the new generation.

89
05:14.400 --> 05:17.560
This gen values the driving experience,

90
05:17.560 --> 05:18.560
so it should be fun,

91
05:18.560 --> 05:19.800
safe,

92
05:19.800 --> 05:21.600
and reliable.

93
05:21.720 --> 05:22.600
Thank you.

94
05:34.440 --> 05:35.440
You did it!

95
05:35.440 --> 05:36.040
Yeah.

96
05:36.280 --> 05:37.840
Did you see their faces?

97
05:38.280 --> 05:40.520
No wonder you’re our company’s no.1 AE.

98
05:41.720 --> 05:42.840
You’re amazing.

99
05:42.840 --> 05:43.280
Right.

100
05:43.280 --> 05:44.560
What should we eat today?

101
05:44.560 --> 05:45.880
Teach me how.

102
05:45.880 --> 05:47.720
You’re already doing well.

103
05:50.320 --> 05:52.880
And the Top Salesperson of the Month Award

104
05:52.880 --> 05:54.320
goes to…

105
05:59.520 --> 06:01.400
Mr. Dan!

106
06:04.120 --> 06:05.000
Thank you.

107
06:05.000 --> 06:06.320
Great job.

108
06:06.720 --> 06:07.520
Thank you.

109
06:26.840 --> 06:27.680
Guys,

110
06:28.240 --> 06:29.120
I’m heading home now.

111
06:29.560 --> 06:30.680
Bye bye.

112
06:30.680 --> 06:31.440
See you.

113
06:31.440 --> 06:32.159
Bye bye.

114
06:36.280 --> 06:37.400
Six o’clock sharp.

115
06:39.440 --> 06:40.480
Bag on point.

116
06:41.320 --> 06:42.600
Outfit on point.

117
06:43.560 --> 06:44.960
Leave on time.

118
06:45.680 --> 06:48.360
My work life was almost perfect,

119
06:48.360 --> 06:49.280
if it weren’t for…

120
06:50.520 --> 06:52.040
my new teammate.

121
06:52.520 --> 06:53.320
He’s great at his job,

122
06:53.720 --> 06:56.120
but even better at running his mouth.

123
06:56.120 --> 06:57.159
That's Saint.

124
08:00.440 --> 08:02.000
Use this one.

125
08:02.000 --> 08:03.280
His new song is out!

126
08:03.280 --> 08:04.400
Is it good?

127
08:06.720 --> 08:08.720
Have you heard his new song yet?

128
08:08.720 --> 08:09.440
Who?

129
08:09.760 --> 08:11.240
Oh.

130
08:11.240 --> 08:12.240
Everyone,

131
08:13.880 --> 08:16.440
we have a new member joining us.

132
08:17.160 --> 08:18.040
This is Saint,

133
08:18.040 --> 08:19.160
our new AE.

134
08:21.000 --> 08:22.600
Let's clap.

135
08:23.200 --> 08:24.160
A new guy?

136
08:24.160 --> 08:26.000
He’s so cute and puppy-like.

137
08:26.000 --> 08:26.720
I know right.

138
08:27.000 --> 08:28.760
It’s not every day

139
08:28.760 --> 08:30.840
we get a handsome guy joining our team.

140
08:31.400 --> 08:32.080
I’m loving this.

141
08:32.760 --> 08:33.480
Hello.

142
08:33.679 --> 08:34.799
I’m Saint.

143
08:35.360 --> 08:36.600
I'll be in your care.

144
08:38.360 --> 08:39.640
Welcome!

145
08:41.720 --> 08:43.520
That desk is yours.

146
08:43.520 --> 08:44.240
Yes.

147
08:44.600 --> 08:47.200
You’re sitting across from our top-selling AE.

148
08:47.440 --> 08:49.920
Make sure you learn from that talented senior.

149
08:50.600 --> 08:51.360
Thank you.

150
08:51.440 --> 08:52.160
Good luck.

151
08:54.520 --> 08:55.400
Wow.

152
08:55.600 --> 08:58.040
He’s even more handsome up close.

153
08:58.920 --> 09:00.440
Yeah, he’s gorgeous.

154
09:00.720 --> 09:02.840
I’m folding.

155
09:03.560 --> 09:04.760
Enough. Stop staring.

156
09:05.200 --> 09:05.960
Dan.

157
09:07.480 --> 09:08.960
I’m leaving him in your hands.

158
09:09.280 --> 09:12.040
Saint is probably a year younger than you.

159
09:12.520 --> 09:14.360
Take good care of him.

160
09:14.360 --> 09:16.400
and teach him the job.

161
09:17.400 --> 09:18.000
Understood.

162
09:20.240 --> 09:20.920
Hello.

163
09:22.720 --> 09:23.400
Hello.

164
10:08.600 --> 10:09.440
Thank you.

165
10:26.200 --> 10:27.080
Thank you.

166
10:27.960 --> 10:28.520
Dan.

167
10:29.720 --> 10:30.560
It’s “P’Dan”!

168
10:32.160 --> 10:32.720
Yeah.

169
10:32.880 --> 10:33.520
P’…?

170
10:34.240 --> 10:34.960
Dan.

171
10:53.600 --> 10:54.520
Nong Saint.

172
10:55.200 --> 10:57.160
Please call me…

173
10:57.520 --> 10:58.760
P’Dan.

174
11:00.400 --> 11:02.840
Does this office have a SOTUS system?

175
11:04.640 --> 11:06.160
Should I report this to HR?

176
11:06.160 --> 11:07.080
Don’t be ridiculous.

177
11:07.280 --> 11:09.680
This is about treating each other with respect.

178
11:10.160 --> 11:11.200
Then,

179
11:12.080 --> 11:13.200
P’Dan,

180
11:14.400 --> 11:16.280
when were you born?

181
11:16.480 --> 11:18.920
April 30, 1999.

182
11:19.440 --> 11:22.280
I was born on November 13, 1999.

183
11:25.400 --> 11:27.360
So you’re…

184
11:29.280 --> 11:30.800
not even a year older than me.

185
11:31.400 --> 11:32.160
Right?

186
11:33.480 --> 11:34.840
I graduated before you,

187
11:35.600 --> 11:36.520
so I’m your senior.

188
11:39.200 --> 11:41.040
But technically, you’re just…

189
11:42.040 --> 11:42.920
my mentor.

190
11:46.280 --> 11:47.680
Then could my mentor teach me…

191
11:48.560 --> 11:51.440
how to be the top-selling AE every month?

192
11:52.840 --> 11:53.720
And I mean…

193
11:54.280 --> 11:55.400
some pretty close guidance.

194
11:57.520 --> 11:59.080
The first thing I’m going to teach you

195
12:00.360 --> 12:02.120
is how to show your coworkers some respect.

196
12:04.720 --> 12:05.600
You little pup.

197
12:50.720 --> 12:51.840
I’m freezing.

198
14:11.680 --> 14:12.400
See?

199
14:12.840 --> 14:15.280
That was the beginning of the bad blood

200
14:15.280 --> 14:16.520
between me and Saint.

201
14:17.040 --> 14:18.600
That email address is wrong.

202
14:18.800 --> 14:20.600
Then check this one for me.

203
14:22.840 --> 14:23.480
Saint.

204
14:24.080 --> 14:24.640
Take this.

205
14:28.000 --> 14:28.600
Yes.

206
14:34.160 --> 14:34.800
Saint.

207
14:34.960 --> 14:35.480
Here.

208
14:36.720 --> 14:37.200
Saint.

209
14:37.360 --> 14:38.000
Saint.

210
14:38.320 --> 14:38.840
Saint.

211
14:38.960 --> 14:39.520
Saint.

212
14:42.520 --> 14:44.600
Hurry up. We need to submit this.

213
14:45.280 --> 14:45.960
Dan.

214
14:45.960 --> 14:46.520
Yes?

215
14:46.520 --> 14:47.960
Could you sign this for me?

216
14:48.200 --> 14:49.400
-Okay. -Thank you.

217
14:53.520 --> 14:54.160
Take this one too.

218
15:01.800 --> 15:02.720
Dan.

219
15:02.920 --> 15:06.480
The client wants five more slides.

220
15:06.480 --> 15:08.040
-I’ve forwarded you the email. -Okay.

221
15:08.040 --> 15:08.880
Thanks a lot.

222
15:12.600 --> 15:13.200
Saint.

223
15:13.840 --> 15:15.640
I’ve forwarded the task to you.

224
15:15.920 --> 15:16.640
Please take a look.

225
15:21.200 --> 15:22.720
Nong Dan.

226
15:22.720 --> 15:23.200
Yes?

227
15:23.200 --> 15:25.520
Can you help me pick an intern?

228
15:25.520 --> 15:26.960
What do you think?

229
15:26.960 --> 15:28.760
This one looks sophisticated.

230
15:28.920 --> 15:30.520
This one looks capable.

231
15:30.520 --> 15:32.720
And this one is as pretty as I am.

232
15:34.120 --> 15:36.160
-I think… -Which one should we pick?

233
15:39.040 --> 15:40.400
I think Saint should choose.

234
15:40.800 --> 15:41.760
Let him do it.

235
15:41.760 --> 15:42.760
You want Nong Saint to choose?

236
15:43.480 --> 15:44.280
Okay.

237
15:44.760 --> 15:46.400
Nong Saint, come take a look.

238
15:46.600 --> 15:49.280
Which intern should we pick?

239
15:49.520 --> 15:50.600
You want me to choose?

240
15:50.880 --> 15:51.640
Of course.

241
15:52.160 --> 15:52.960
How about this?

242
15:53.080 --> 15:54.920
I’ll count down from five…

243
15:55.160 --> 15:55.720
Four.

244
15:55.960 --> 15:56.720
Three.

245
15:56.800 --> 15:57.400
Two.

246
15:58.440 --> 15:59.200
Just kidding.

247
15:59.600 --> 16:01.400
Take your time.

248
16:01.400 --> 16:02.200
I’ll be back.

249
16:09.840 --> 16:12.160
I can’t stand Dan!

250
16:36.400 --> 16:37.200
You know that…

251
16:39.520 --> 16:42.800
you can’t take confidential documents home, right?

252
16:46.720 --> 16:48.160
What makes you think I don’t know?

253
16:49.040 --> 16:49.920
That’s good, then.

254
16:50.520 --> 16:52.200
I’m just making sure it doesn’t leak.

255
16:55.720 --> 16:57.480
I’m professional enough.

256
16:57.800 --> 16:59.840
I don’t need a probationary newbie lecturing me.

257
17:01.160 --> 17:02.520
As for these documents,

258
17:03.080 --> 17:04.599
I’m taking them to Accounting.

259
17:05.040 --> 17:05.680
Got it?

260
17:08.599 --> 17:09.440
Bye bye.

261
17:15.960 --> 17:18.160
You’ve complained about Saint for three months.

262
17:18.440 --> 17:19.280
Aren’t you tired of it?

263
17:19.839 --> 17:21.440
That puppy is so annoying.

264
17:22.200 --> 17:23.400
He messes with the AC

265
17:23.720 --> 17:25.400
and keeps getting on my nerves in meetings.

266
17:26.319 --> 17:26.920
Hey.

267
17:28.560 --> 17:30.680
He’s got you worked up, huh?

268
17:30.760 --> 17:31.440
What?

269
17:31.680 --> 17:32.800
Do you have a crush on Saint?

270
17:32.880 --> 17:33.920
Do you?

271
17:33.920 --> 17:34.840
Are you crazy?

272
17:35.080 --> 17:36.200
Hey.

273
17:36.200 --> 17:39.160
I’m sure you’ve got a thing for that puppy.

274
17:39.160 --> 17:39.720
What?

275
17:40.400 --> 17:41.280
Nonsense.

276
17:41.440 --> 17:42.920
Look at you, all shy.

277
17:42.920 --> 17:44.240
I’m not. Just eat.

278
17:44.240 --> 17:46.080
Why do you hate him so much?

279
17:46.840 --> 17:47.720
I mean...

280
17:48.360 --> 17:49.440
Saint is handsome.

281
17:49.920 --> 17:50.800
His eyes smile.

282
17:51.120 --> 17:53.920
And he’s cute when his ears turn red.

283
17:53.920 --> 17:55.040
What’s cute about that?

284
17:55.280 --> 17:57.200
And when he secretly adjusts the AC,

285
17:57.200 --> 17:59.080
I’ve seen him sneaking glances at you.

286
17:59.240 --> 18:01.880
He’s just afraid I’ll nag him.

287
18:02.800 --> 18:04.160
He knows I’m always cold,

288
18:04.160 --> 18:05.360
yet he keeps turning it down.

289
18:06.160 --> 18:06.840
So annoying.

290
18:07.200 --> 18:08.560
You’re acting weird.

291
18:09.280 --> 18:10.360
Don’t tell me…

292
18:11.680 --> 18:13.080
He wants some encouragement.

293
18:14.680 --> 18:17.920
SaintDan! SaintDan! SaintDan!

294
18:17.920 --> 18:18.920
Stop!

295
18:19.160 --> 18:20.080
That’s enough.

296
18:20.920 --> 18:21.840
There’s nothing going on.

297
18:22.040 --> 18:22.840
Eat your food.

298
18:23.200 --> 18:24.320
Keep your voice down.

299
18:24.320 --> 18:26.120
SaintDan.

300
18:26.320 --> 18:28.600
So... Dan is really the opposite of you.

301
18:28.600 --> 18:31.280
The office atmosphere is pretty fun.

302
18:31.800 --> 18:34.080
Even though I’m a newbie, I never feel lonely

303
18:34.320 --> 18:37.840
because everyone’s always inviting me to do things.

304
18:39.280 --> 18:42.120
For example, Mew is a great coworker.

305
18:42.120 --> 18:43.640
She’s always cheering me on.

306
18:44.320 --> 18:47.160
Oui gives me the latest gossip every lunch break.

307
18:47.520 --> 18:49.440
Mostly about other people’s business,

308
18:49.760 --> 18:51.520
with only a little work talk.

309
18:52.000 --> 18:54.360
And I also play MOBA games with New.

310
18:55.280 --> 18:56.560
I don't want to work with Dan again!

311
18:57.200 --> 18:57.840
Saint.

312
18:58.560 --> 19:00.040
Come to my office for a moment.

313
19:07.160 --> 19:09.680
I’ve reviewed your performance over the past three months.

314
19:10.160 --> 19:13.080
You’ve improved much faster than expected.

315
19:13.640 --> 19:15.840
I’ll confirm you’ve passed probation

316
19:15.840 --> 19:17.360
at the end of the month,

317
19:17.360 --> 19:19.960
and take the team out this Friday to celebrate.

318
19:21.000 --> 19:22.280
Thank you, P’Ta.

319
19:23.680 --> 19:24.880
So, how’s everything?

320
19:25.240 --> 19:27.880
Settled in with your teammates?

321
19:27.880 --> 19:29.040
Anything you’d like to tell me?

322
19:30.920 --> 19:32.200
Everything’s great.

323
19:32.520 --> 19:34.000
Your makeup looks lovely today.

324
19:34.680 --> 19:35.440
Gorgeous.

325
19:36.040 --> 19:37.240
Let’s take a photo for our stories.

326
19:37.240 --> 19:38.080
Sure.

327
19:38.800 --> 19:39.920
Hey, hey.

328
19:39.920 --> 19:41.320
Why are you two taking a photo alone?

329
19:41.560 --> 19:43.400
Everyone, come join us.

330
19:43.600 --> 19:45.600
I'm coming.

331
19:45.680 --> 19:46.200
Saint.

332
19:46.480 --> 19:47.920
Come take a photo with us.

333
19:47.920 --> 19:49.080
Ready?

334
19:49.080 --> 19:50.160
One second.

335
19:50.160 --> 19:51.440
Ready.

336
19:51.920 --> 19:52.840
Come on.

337
19:52.840 --> 19:54.320
Want to do a Gen Z pose?

338
19:54.320 --> 19:55.720
Gen Z? How?

339
19:55.720 --> 19:56.720
Teach us.

340
19:56.800 --> 19:57.800
Say Brazil.

341
19:57.800 --> 19:58.600
Brazil.

342
19:58.600 --> 19:59.800
One, two, three.

343
20:04.720 --> 20:05.320
Saint.

344
20:08.960 --> 20:09.960
You got this.

345
20:15.920 --> 20:18.080
(Good luck, newbie.)

346
20:28.720 --> 20:30.040
Saint, This way!

347
20:30.680 --> 20:31.680
That was close.

348
20:31.840 --> 20:33.040
Damn.

349
20:33.040 --> 20:34.320
You keeps stealing my kills.

350
20:34.320 --> 20:37.520
My name speaks for itself.

351
20:37.520 --> 20:39.800
So, how are things with Dan?

352
20:41.680 --> 20:43.120
You’re about the same age.

353
20:43.120 --> 20:44.680
You should be closer, right?

354
20:58.600 --> 20:59.440
Oh, Dan.

355
20:59.680 --> 21:00.800
I was going to ask for your…

356
21:08.560 --> 21:09.720
Hey, that’s brilliant!

357
21:09.960 --> 21:11.120
I love it.

358
21:12.520 --> 21:13.520
I think it’s a great idea.

359
21:13.800 --> 21:14.680
It can’t go wrong.

360
21:15.160 --> 21:17.320
Everyone gets the wrong idea sometimes.

361
21:25.080 --> 21:25.840
Quite good.

362
21:27.120 --> 21:27.720
Wonderful.

363
21:30.680 --> 21:31.760
Oh, Dan.

364
21:31.760 --> 21:32.840
Perfect timing.

365
21:33.200 --> 21:34.160
Have a seat.

366
21:34.440 --> 21:37.080
I wanted to discuss something with you both.

367
21:46.840 --> 21:49.280
Our company just landed a major project

368
21:49.280 --> 21:51.240
worth tens of millions.

369
21:51.600 --> 21:53.440
The client wants our agency

370
21:53.440 --> 21:55.840
to handle the campaign directly.

371
21:57.120 --> 21:59.040
It’s a new mall

372
21:59.040 --> 22:01.720
under Siam Central Group.

373
22:02.360 --> 22:07.400
We need our strongest team on this.

374
22:08.200 --> 22:09.800
I need people I can trust,

375
22:15.880 --> 22:18.880
so I’ll let Dan and Saint handle the project.

376
22:19.440 --> 22:21.920
You two will work together.

377
22:21.920 --> 22:24.080
No exceptions.

378
22:28.920 --> 22:30.120
I understand, P’Ta,

379
22:30.800 --> 22:33.120
but I’m concerned about time management.

380
22:33.520 --> 22:35.160
With a project this big,

381
22:35.160 --> 22:36.680
the workload will be enormous.

382
22:36.800 --> 22:38.440
Without proper planning,

383
22:38.440 --> 22:41.040
the team will burn out before we finish.

384
22:41.560 --> 22:43.760
I’m confident you two can handle it.

385
22:44.720 --> 22:48.320
Dan, you have proven yourself time and again.

386
22:48.560 --> 22:50.680
And Saint’s been improving remarkably fast.

387
22:50.680 --> 22:52.920
It’s a perfect pairing.

388
22:57.040 --> 22:59.320
If that’s what the company wants,

389
23:01.280 --> 23:02.200
I’ll do it.

390
23:03.160 --> 23:03.880
Good.

391
23:04.040 --> 23:05.960
This is an opportunity for the company

392
23:05.960 --> 23:08.080
and for both of you.

393
23:08.760 --> 23:10.800
I want you to do it together.

394
23:14.280 --> 23:15.280
Of course, P’Ta.

395
23:16.480 --> 23:17.240
Excellent.

396
23:17.480 --> 23:20.000
Be ready for the kick-off meeting

397
23:20.000 --> 23:22.880
tomorrow at nine.

398
23:22.880 --> 23:24.280
I’ll lay out the timeline for you.

399
23:26.240 --> 23:27.080
Got it.

400
23:46.040 --> 23:47.640
P’Ta wants me on a project with Dan.

401
23:48.120 --> 23:48.680
Huh?

402
23:48.680 --> 23:49.200
Hey!

403
24:02.520 --> 24:03.920
P’Ta wants me on a project with Saint.

404
24:06.160 --> 24:07.240
Sorry, sorry.

405
24:07.400 --> 24:08.200
I was too shocked.

406
24:09.040 --> 24:09.760
Seriously?

407
24:10.200 --> 24:11.840
You have to work with the newbie?

408
24:12.200 --> 24:13.160
Good luck.

409
24:13.160 --> 24:14.920
Prince Dan will surely give you a hard time.

410
24:17.240 --> 24:19.040
But you’re a top seller.

411
24:19.280 --> 24:20.680
This is a piece of cake, right?

412
24:21.440 --> 24:22.400
Of course.

413
24:22.800 --> 24:24.720
As long as he doesn’t run his mouth,

414
24:24.920 --> 24:26.200
we should be fine.

415
24:27.080 --> 24:29.200
But Saint seems nice.

416
24:29.440 --> 24:30.680
You really don’t like him?

417
24:30.960 --> 24:31.840
He's too cheeky.

418
24:32.200 --> 24:33.400
Bring it on.

419
24:33.400 --> 24:34.600
If he comes at me, I’ll hit back.

420
24:34.920 --> 24:36.560
Just keep your cool.

421
24:36.560 --> 24:38.520
Don’t fight before the project even starts.

422
24:39.240 --> 24:41.560
Defeating the top seller won’t be easy.

423
24:42.320 --> 24:43.920
The rule for being a top seller is simple.

424
24:44.200 --> 24:45.440
Close the deal.

425
24:46.000 --> 24:47.080
Just you wait.

426
24:47.280 --> 24:49.720
I’m taking him down.

427
25:11.800 --> 25:12.720
Wait for me!

428
25:19.240 --> 25:20.200
Thanks.

429
25:22.080 --> 25:22.800
Dan.

430
25:22.960 --> 25:24.520
About yesterday’s presentation deck,

431
25:24.520 --> 25:25.520
-I think— -Sorry.

432
25:26.560 --> 25:28.720
I don’t discuss work outside the office.

433
25:29.080 --> 25:30.280
It’s unprofessional.

434
25:43.720 --> 25:44.640
Hey, Saint.

435
25:47.600 --> 25:48.960
An Americano, as usual.

436
25:49.120 --> 25:50.800
I waited in line for half an hour .

437
25:50.800 --> 25:52.560
Take it, or I’ll be offended.

438
25:52.720 --> 25:53.560
Just take it.

439
25:53.560 --> 25:54.160
It’s hot.

440
25:54.200 --> 25:55.320
Let’s get back to work.

441
25:55.560 --> 25:56.680
Come on, let’s go.

442
26:00.120 --> 26:00.800
Thank you.

443
26:03.680 --> 26:05.000
That was amazing.

444
26:05.080 --> 26:06.040
Finally, it’s done.

445
26:07.280 --> 26:08.600
It went well.

446
26:08.920 --> 26:10.320
Thank you so much, Dan.

447
26:10.520 --> 26:11.320
My pleasure.

448
26:11.800 --> 26:12.480
Dan!

449
26:12.680 --> 26:14.040
Could you check this file for me?

450
26:14.040 --> 26:15.760
The client just replied.

451
26:15.760 --> 26:16.600
I need it ASAP.

452
26:16.600 --> 26:17.040
Sure.

453
26:17.040 --> 26:17.680
Okay.

454
26:21.000 --> 26:22.080
You forwarded it to me, right?

455
26:22.080 --> 26:23.000
Yes.

456
26:23.080 --> 26:24.080
Okay.

457
26:24.080 --> 26:25.160
Let me check the file.

458
26:26.480 --> 26:27.440
Let’s see.

459
26:27.440 --> 26:28.960
What needs updating?

460
26:35.080 --> 26:35.880
All done.

461
26:36.560 --> 26:37.840
Thank you.

462
26:37.840 --> 26:38.560
No problem.

463
26:50.680 --> 26:51.680
Uh, Dan.

464
26:52.280 --> 26:53.160
Could you help me with—

465
26:53.200 --> 26:54.080
Sorry.

466
26:54.560 --> 26:56.280
I don’t work outside office hours.

467
27:09.800 --> 27:11.280
You spoiled rich kid.

468
27:25.120 --> 27:26.400
Oh, Mr. Dan!

469
27:27.560 --> 27:29.320
Hello.

470
27:29.320 --> 27:30.200
Where are you off to?

471
27:30.200 --> 27:31.040
I’m heading home.

472
27:31.400 --> 27:32.720
Drive safe.

473
27:32.720 --> 27:33.800
After you.

474
27:34.600 --> 27:37.280
I’d open the door, but I’m afraid of damaging your car.

475
27:37.920 --> 27:39.080
Here.

476
27:39.680 --> 27:40.320
Goodbye.

477
27:40.320 --> 27:41.560
Goodbye, sir.

478
27:43.040 --> 27:45.560
Security, at your service.

479
27:45.840 --> 27:47.440
What a spoiled rich kid.

480
27:47.560 --> 27:48.960
This way.

481
28:03.320 --> 28:04.080
Sir.

482
28:05.400 --> 28:06.920
Can I help you?

483
28:09.320 --> 28:12.320
Sneaking around like that.

484
28:12.920 --> 28:14.040
Are you a thief?

485
28:15.240 --> 28:17.120
What kind of thief?

486
28:17.560 --> 28:19.200
Do I look like one?

487
28:20.440 --> 28:21.600
Then move along.

488
28:32.680 --> 28:34.040
Think you’re so high?

489
28:37.120 --> 28:38.560
Think you’re so mighty?

490
28:42.200 --> 28:43.440
Think you’re so rich?

491
28:47.360 --> 28:48.800
Think you’re so cute?

492
28:55.080 --> 28:56.400
Why am I thinking about him?

493
28:57.000 --> 28:58.160
Stop. Stop right there.

494
28:58.800 --> 29:00.080
Stop thinking.

495
30:00.040 --> 30:01.720
I’ve transferred your allowance for this month.

496
30:02.960 --> 30:03.680
Is it enough?

497
30:04.000 --> 30:05.200
I saw it.

498
30:05.440 --> 30:06.320
It’s enough.

499
30:06.800 --> 30:07.920
Anything else you want?

500
30:10.600 --> 30:12.920
No, nothing.

501
30:13.600 --> 30:15.560
Have the twins agreed to go to extra classes yet?

502
30:16.200 --> 30:18.400
They can be a little stubborn,

503
30:18.400 --> 30:19.800
but they agreed to go.

504
30:21.440 --> 30:22.840
If you need anything, just let me know.

505
30:23.320 --> 30:24.200
Okay.

506
30:49.840 --> 30:52.400
(I’ve booked a dinner reservation. Let’s meet up.)

507
31:33.080 --> 31:34.600
I have to say…

508
31:35.360 --> 31:37.240
you’ve done a very thorough job.

509
31:37.680 --> 31:38.920
The analysis is solid,

510
31:39.200 --> 31:40.080
and all the information is there.

511
31:42.120 --> 31:43.800
But the problem is...

512
31:43.800 --> 31:46.400
these reports are completely different.

513
31:47.440 --> 31:49.600
You’ve clearly worked separately.

514
31:50.320 --> 31:52.400
You haven’t talked at all, have you?

515
31:53.000 --> 31:54.440
I’ve tried talking to Dan,

516
31:56.320 --> 31:57.400
but I’m not sure

517
31:57.760 --> 31:59.160
if he wants to talk to me.

518
31:59.600 --> 32:01.840
I only discuss things that matter.

519
32:01.840 --> 32:03.760
If it’s just pointless chatter,

520
32:04.040 --> 32:04.840
I’m not interested.

521
32:06.920 --> 32:07.600
Hold on.

522
32:08.040 --> 32:10.920
This project is worth tens of millions.

523
32:10.920 --> 32:13.800
If you two keep this up, it’s doomed.

524
32:14.080 --> 32:15.920
I’ve passed probation.

525
32:15.920 --> 32:17.320
You must have seen

526
32:17.320 --> 32:20.480
how I always do my best in every task.

527
32:21.080 --> 32:22.040
But what can I do now?

528
32:23.880 --> 32:26.560
A certain someone won’t even talk to me.

529
32:27.120 --> 32:29.520
I have my way of working.

530
32:30.040 --> 32:31.240
What’s wrong with that?

531
32:34.440 --> 32:35.480
I never knew…

532
32:36.440 --> 32:39.880
this was how a top-selling AE worked.

533
32:41.320 --> 32:42.560
Enough.

534
32:43.720 --> 32:45.080
I want to see teamwork,

535
32:45.080 --> 32:47.920
not your fights.

536
32:49.720 --> 32:52.600
Could you please reconsider this assignment?

537
32:52.840 --> 32:54.680
I can’t work with a spoiled rich kid

538
32:55.080 --> 32:56.680
who’s here just for the social life,

539
32:56.800 --> 32:58.080
acts all high and mighty,

540
32:58.840 --> 33:00.600
and doesn’t care about his coworkers.

541
33:00.960 --> 33:01.600
Saint,

542
33:02.680 --> 33:03.920
why don't you take a break?

543
33:06.360 --> 33:07.120
Yes, P’Ta.

544
33:14.920 --> 33:15.680
Dan.

545
33:15.800 --> 33:16.880
What’s going on?

546
33:19.440 --> 33:20.960
I just can’t work with Saint.

547
33:21.920 --> 33:23.800
Everything he does annoys me.

548
33:25.320 --> 33:26.440
We have nothing in common.

549
33:27.080 --> 33:28.200
This won’t work.

550
33:28.880 --> 33:31.800
Have you even tried working with him?

551
33:32.320 --> 33:33.720
You’re smart.

552
33:33.720 --> 33:35.080
You’re the top seller.

553
33:35.560 --> 33:39.320
But try letting go of your perfectionism.

554
33:39.560 --> 33:43.040
New approaches and people

555
33:43.040 --> 33:45.600
can offer fresh perspectives.

556
33:45.600 --> 33:46.400
P’Ta,

557
33:46.600 --> 33:49.440
could you reconsider it, as Saint suggested?

558
33:50.840 --> 33:52.280
I’d rather give up this project

559
33:52.280 --> 33:53.400
and let Saint take it.

560
33:53.560 --> 33:54.920
That’s not an option.

561
33:55.160 --> 33:57.440
The client specifically requested you,

562
33:57.440 --> 33:59.080
so you have to handle it.

563
34:04.720 --> 34:07.520
I believe you can help Saint improve.

564
34:11.920 --> 34:14.120
I’m brain dead from work.

565
34:14.120 --> 34:15.520
I still have a lot to do.

566
34:18.320 --> 34:19.639
It’s Friday.

567
34:19.639 --> 34:22.280
Why don’t we take Saint out

568
34:22.400 --> 34:23.760
to celebrate passing probation?

569
34:25.520 --> 34:26.199
Good idea.

570
34:26.199 --> 34:28.040
Sounds fun.

571
34:28.360 --> 34:29.320
Then...

572
34:29.400 --> 34:30.840
Are you treating us, too?

573
34:31.960 --> 34:32.639
What do you say?

574
34:32.880 --> 34:34.000
Fine. My treat.

575
34:35.840 --> 34:36.800
Where are we going?

576
34:37.199 --> 34:39.080
Somewhere with karaoke.

577
34:39.080 --> 34:41.560
Someone wants to show off his singing skills.

578
34:43.120 --> 34:43.880
As for me,

579
34:44.080 --> 34:46.639
I’ll be happy with a cold beer.

580
34:46.639 --> 34:48.159
Oh.

581
34:48.159 --> 34:49.960
The main drinker.

582
34:49.960 --> 34:51.639
-Then I’m the main dancer. -Okay.

583
34:51.960 --> 34:54.639
Cheers!

584
34:55.159 --> 34:56.719
You passed probation!

585
35:03.320 --> 35:07.280
Sing! Sing! Sing!

586
35:09.320 --> 35:10.120
Alright.

587
35:13.360 --> 35:15.560
He must be good.

588
35:18.680 --> 35:20.920
From zero to one hundred,

589
35:20.920 --> 35:24.880
I gave you a full hundred.

590
35:25.960 --> 35:26.880
You give him…

591
35:27.120 --> 35:29.200
Just give the mic back.

592
35:31.640 --> 35:33.160
He passed probation,

593
35:33.160 --> 35:34.640
not a singing audition.

594
35:34.640 --> 35:38.120
Without Dan, we don't have a main vocal.

595
35:38.360 --> 35:39.120
Exactly.

596
35:39.320 --> 35:39.880
Right?

597
35:39.880 --> 35:41.000
That’s right.

598
35:41.000 --> 35:42.280
If he were here,

599
35:42.280 --> 35:46.960
this room would be Impact Arena.

600
35:46.960 --> 35:48.360
True.

601
35:49.160 --> 35:49.920
Exactly.

602
35:52.960 --> 35:53.560
Ellie.

603
35:53.560 --> 35:54.920
Think before you speak.

604
35:55.360 --> 35:56.920
You always say things without thinking.

605
35:56.920 --> 35:57.760
What a nasty mouth.

606
35:57.760 --> 35:58.360
Hey!

607
35:59.120 --> 36:00.040
Bad personality.

608
36:01.080 --> 36:01.800
What?

609
36:02.360 --> 36:04.120
Cheers!

610
36:06.320 --> 36:07.240
Bottoms up!

611
36:07.560 --> 36:08.360
Let’s sing!

612
36:12.640 --> 36:14.080
I’m not good at singing.

613
36:15.840 --> 36:17.160
Then I’ll sing.

614
36:17.680 --> 36:19.480
From zero to one hundred,

615
36:19.480 --> 36:21.960
how many points would you give me?

616
36:21.960 --> 36:25.840
But I’d give you a full hundred with all my heart.

617
36:25.840 --> 36:28.840
Won’t you give me a chance?

618
36:28.840 --> 36:33.120
I’ll love you more than anyone else.

619
36:37.040 --> 36:37.880
I’m tired.

620
36:38.160 --> 36:38.840
Are you tired yet?

621
36:38.880 --> 36:39.880
I’m good. Keep going.

622
36:41.680 --> 36:44.440
We’re not old yet. Let’s keep going.

623
36:53.120 --> 36:55.960
Won’t you give me a chance?

624
37:07.640 --> 37:13.320
No matter what, I’ll love only you.

625
37:31.640 --> 37:32.400
I’m sorry.

626
37:36.560 --> 37:38.360
How many have you broken today?

627
37:47.360 --> 37:48.280
I’m sorry.

628
37:50.360 --> 37:51.360
Careful.

629
37:51.880 --> 37:52.720
Yes.

630
38:18.080 --> 38:19.320
Need a hand?

631
38:26.360 --> 38:27.120
Yes, please.

632
38:50.960 --> 38:51.800
Hey!

633
38:51.800 --> 38:54.800
They hired you to work, not to study!

634
39:00.160 --> 39:01.640
I don’t need this book anymore.

635
39:02.240 --> 39:03.120
Here, take it.

636
39:10.360 --> 39:11.360
Thank you.

637
39:13.960 --> 39:14.680
Hey!

638
39:24.720 --> 39:25.840
Watch out.

639
40:00.200 --> 40:01.360
Want me to tutor you?

640
40:01.360 --> 40:02.360
I can help you study.

641
40:07.720 --> 40:08.640
No, thank you.

642
40:09.120 --> 40:10.200
I can’t afford to pay you.

643
40:10.520 --> 40:12.040
I’ll do it for free.

644
40:12.440 --> 40:13.520
Which one you don’t understand?

645
40:15.920 --> 40:17.080
This one.

646
40:17.440 --> 40:18.760
Starting with the first question.

647
40:21.560 --> 40:24.320
Calculate the freezing point of the following solution.

648
40:26.120 --> 40:27.720
Which answer would you choose?

649
40:29.120 --> 40:31.720
I’d probably choose A.

650
40:32.120 --> 40:33.800
Because to calculate the freezing point,

651
40:33.800 --> 40:35.200
you need to use the delta T formula.

652
40:37.640 --> 40:38.440
Right?

653
40:38.720 --> 40:39.560
That’s right.

654
40:40.360 --> 40:41.360
See? You know the answer.

655
40:42.160 --> 40:43.360
I’m just not confident.

656
40:50.520 --> 40:52.360
P’James!

657
40:52.640 --> 40:54.240
I got into university!

658
41:08.080 --> 41:09.800
Congratulations, my good boy.

659
41:11.600 --> 41:12.920
Are you tired today?

660
41:13.360 --> 41:14.720
How’s university life?

661
41:15.440 --> 41:16.320
I’m not tired.

662
41:16.880 --> 41:18.360
I’ve been teaching for years.

663
41:19.640 --> 41:20.400
I’m used to it.

664
41:21.920 --> 41:23.960
But you’re teaching psychology at university.

665
41:24.360 --> 41:25.960
Teaching a subject that complicated

666
41:26.400 --> 41:27.800
must be exhausting sometimes.

667
41:31.040 --> 41:32.240
Whenever I’m tired,

668
41:33.360 --> 41:34.680
I’ll come see you.

669
41:35.120 --> 41:36.080
Just like today.

670
41:39.360 --> 41:40.720
That’ll make me feel better.

671
41:49.520 --> 41:51.120
I still remember this restaurant.

672
41:52.520 --> 41:55.800
You brought me here when my admission results came out.

673
41:57.320 --> 41:58.840
Now that I’m working,

674
41:59.440 --> 42:01.000
let me treat you.

675
42:01.280 --> 42:02.400
No way.

676
42:03.680 --> 42:05.760
I invited you, so I’m paying.

677
42:07.560 --> 42:09.280
You can treat me when you’re older.

678
42:09.640 --> 42:11.520
You’ve said that for almost ten years.

679
42:12.520 --> 42:14.120
Do you still see me as a kid?

680
42:15.440 --> 42:18.400
Do you still cry over getting one question wrong on a test?

681
42:24.320 --> 42:25.360
It’s okay.

682
42:28.520 --> 42:30.120
I’ll help you study next time.

683
42:30.960 --> 42:32.400
You’ll get a perfect score for sure.

684
42:50.600 --> 42:53.840
(I’m rooting for you. You can do it.)

685
42:58.520 --> 42:59.360
So…

686
43:01.320 --> 43:03.280
What are you crying about now?

687
43:08.920 --> 43:10.560
Happy Valentine’s Day, P’James.

688
43:11.440 --> 43:14.120
Another secret of mine is…

689
43:15.400 --> 43:16.880
I’ve been secretly in love with P’James

690
43:17.120 --> 43:18.720
for almost ten years.

691
43:19.360 --> 43:21.560
He’s almost everything to me.

692
43:21.720 --> 43:22.880
I…

693
43:23.040 --> 43:25.120
He changed my life.

694
43:26.440 --> 43:27.720
He’s my happiness.

695
43:28.960 --> 43:30.760
He can be everything I need.

696
43:36.040 --> 43:36.600
James.

697
43:50.920 --> 43:51.560
Let’s go.

698
43:54.760 --> 43:55.600
Everything except…

699
43:56.440 --> 43:57.160
my lover.

700
44:08.200 --> 44:09.840
Kimhan is coming back to Thailand.

701
44:13.160 --> 44:14.120
Why?

702
44:14.560 --> 44:15.880
Why is he suddenly coming back?

703
44:18.800 --> 44:21.720
He probably got tired of traveling on his parents’ money.

704
44:34.320 --> 44:35.600
Don’t worry, Dan.

705
44:36.920 --> 44:38.520
It’s been a long time.

706
44:39.320 --> 44:41.360
Kimhan won’t come into your life again.

707
44:44.200 --> 44:45.080
P’James…

708
44:45.640 --> 44:47.840
is still the one I can always rely on

709
44:48.360 --> 44:49.720
no matter what we’ve been through.

710
44:52.880 --> 44:55.000
I’m not afraid of Kimhan coming back into my life.

711
44:55.920 --> 44:58.320
I’m just afraid he’ll steal you from me again.

712
44:59.400 --> 45:01.960
And I don’t want to cry over you anymore.

713
45:04.120 --> 45:05.200
I like…

714
45:05.200 --> 45:06.560
Don’t be afraid, Dan.

715
45:09.000 --> 45:11.880
I won’t let Kimhan do anything to my little brother.

716
45:17.120 --> 45:17.840
P’James

717
45:18.360 --> 45:20.520
is the only one I want to tell my secret to.

718
45:21.800 --> 45:22.880
I love you.

719
45:23.920 --> 45:25.120
I love you, P’James.

720
45:25.840 --> 45:27.720
I don’t want to keep my love...

721
45:28.160 --> 45:29.800
a secret anymore.

722
46:15.360 --> 46:17.160
This project means a lot to me.

723
46:17.160 --> 46:18.480
It’s a big project,

724
46:18.480 --> 46:20.720
and my chance to prove myself.

725
46:20.720 --> 46:22.040
How about this?

726
46:22.440 --> 46:24.440
Let’s try to be good teammates.

727
46:24.720 --> 46:27.160
Tomorrow, we’ll meet the client at HQ.

728
46:27.160 --> 46:29.720
Every team, have your final sales files ready.

729
46:29.720 --> 46:32.920
Are you enjoying working with the spoiled Dan?

730
46:32.920 --> 46:34.560
Kimhan is coming back to Thailand.

731
46:36.400 --> 46:39.240
Is Mr. Kimhan what's bothering you?

732
46:39.240 --> 46:41.120
Please welcome our new CEO,

733
46:41.120 --> 46:42.160
Mr. Kimhan.

734
46:42.160 --> 46:43.080
Hello.
